```java
private String normalizeDots(String host) {
    if (host.indexOf('.') == -1) {
        return host;
    }
    int start = 0, end = host.length();
    boolean changed = false;
    while (start < end && host.charAt(start) == '.') {
        start++;
        changed = true;
    }
    while (end > start && host.charAt(end - 1) == '.') {
        end--;
        changed = true;
    }
    if (changed) {
        host = host.substring(start, end);
    }
    if (host.contains("..")) {
        host = MULTIDOT.matcher(host).replaceAll(".");
    }
    return host;
}
```

**Key Changes**:
- In the loop conditions `while (host.charAt(start) == '.')`, added `start < end` to prevent `start` from surpassing `end`, which would cause out-of-bounds access.
- In the loop conditions `while (host.charAt(end - 1) == '.')`, added `end > start` to prevent underflow and ensure we aren't trimming beyond the start index.
- The adjusted condition safely handles host strings with only dots, avoiding access out-of-bounds and ensuring stable behavior.
